; crm.5ba — 5bit CRM data logic (contacts + deals)
; Pure 5bit. No C. No Python.
; The HTTP server is in the 5bit binary bootstrap (serve mode).
; This file defines the CRM data structures and handlers.
;
; Contact: name, email, phone, company (each stored as a labeled record)
; Deal: title, value, stage, contact_id

def 1
; Contact 1: Alice Johnson, alice@acme.com, 555-0100, Acme Corp
int 0
raw START START START START D5 END END END END D0 END
raw START START START START D5 END END END END
raw START START START START D0 END D1 END D2 END D3 END D4 END END END END
raw END END END END
raw START START START START D5 END END END END
raw END END END END
raw START START START START D5 END END END END D0 END
raw END END END END

; Actually — CRM data should be stored as records in the grid.
; For this demo, we'll embed sample data directly.
; Contact format: WORD(name) NUM(0) WORD(email) NUM(0) WORD(phone) NUM(0) WORD(company) RECORD

; Contact 1
raw START raw START raw START raw START raw D5 END END END END
raw D0 END raw START raw A raw l raw i raw c raw e raw END raw T_POW
raw J raw o raw h raw n raw s raw o raw n raw END raw END
record

record
